const e="uukma-national-kalamela",m=2022,a="Read all 20 pages of the 2022 manual: the foreword (Malayalam, translated; its text uses a legacy font and was read from a page image), contents, introduction, eligibility, age categories and age proof, entry limits, general guidelines, judgement and results, awards and point tables, main changes, list of items by category, complaints, special circumstances, judgement criteria, and the three forms (single item, group item, review form). The manual prints no entry fee, no venue address and no phone numbers; the foreword says the 13th National Kalamela is at Cheltenham on 5 November 2022. The manual prints only names and posts of three officers, kept as a contact variable without phone or email. Conflicts inside the manual are kept as printed and noted: the group size is 3 to 8 in the guidelines but 3 to 10 for Group Song and Nadan Pattukal in the item list; Group Song time is 5 minutes in the guidelines and 7 minutes in the criteria table; Cinematic Group Dance time is 7 minutes in the guidelines and 10 minutes in the criteria table; the introduction says 33 events and six categories, the template Evidence says 43 item-and-age combinations. The template Evidence says every item has five criteria out of 20; the manual prints different criteria and weights per item (each totals 100), which are captured as printed. The template items Singing, Fancy Dress and Katha Prasangam are not named in this manual; Singing is matched to the manual's Kids Solo Song; Fancy Dress and Katha Prasangam have no rows. Not carried by the template and named in `other`: Monoact, Mime, Nadan Pattukal and the Super Seniors category.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"UUKMA Regional and National Kalamela - Kalamela Manual 2022","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Age is taken as on 1 September 2022. Bring proof of age (passport or birth certificate copy or photo). Contestants must report to the stage manager 30 minutes before their slot.","Notes":["Entries are made through the association on the Kalamela web portal.","Time limits are strict: 2 points per judge are deducted for going over time.","Entries for the National Kalamela: three from each region for each individual and group item."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General rules","Items":["UUKMA's Regional and National Kalamela is a competition in Indian traditional art forms for the UK Malayalee community. More than 1,000 participants take part in 33 performing events across six age categories. The event is planned to finish in one day, on 4 to 5 stages.","The aim is to keep the Indian heritage alive by making the ancient art forms popular, and to give young people a platform to show their talent in individual and group competitions.","All single items are common for males and females.","Group events may be performed together or separately by males and females.","Programmes must be of a reasonable standard. Any programme disqualified by the judges is not counted for point allocation.","The organising committee may change any rule, and cancel any event or stage, without notice.","Everyone is asked to co-operate fully (the manual calls this 'a big heart'), as the Kalamela needs the sincere help of contestants, parents and organisers.","The foreword (translated) says the rules are published so that contestants can show their talent without worry, and that the rules were changed after the experience of past years. The foreword says the 13th National Kalamela takes place on {{NationalDate}} at {{NationalVenue}}.","UUKMA asks participants and parents to keep to the high values of our culture when choosing songs and costumes. UUKMA does not support item dances with vulgar content that is not suitable for the age of children."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Who may enter","Items":["Active members of a UUKMA Member Association, and their children, who live in the UK are eligible.","Regional organisers must check that participants are local residents of the Member Association, so the opportunity is not misused.","As a general rule, no professional performers or professional dance teachers may compete in solo or group items, except in Thiruvathira, Oppana and Margamkali.","Age is decided as on {{AgeAsOn}}.","Categories and dates of birth: Kids are 8 years and below (born on or after 1 September 2014). Sub-Juniors are above 8 and up to 12 (born 1 September 2010 to 31 August 2014, both dates included). Juniors are above 12 and up to 17 (born 1 September 2005 to 31 August 2010, both dates included). Seniors are above 17 (born on or before 31 August 2005). Super Seniors are above 35 (born on or before 31 August 1987). Common has no age limit.","No individual may compete in a higher age category if there is a competition for that item in his or her own age category (single and group items).","In group events, the lower age limit may be waived so that children can compete in the next higher group (not the other way). The registration officer must be told. More than half of the participants must be from the age group of the category they compete in. This waiver is not counted for special awards such as championship, Kalathilakam, Kalaprathibha and Natya Mayooram.","Only female teams may take part in Oppana, Thiruvathira and Margam Kali. The songs may be traditional or from films.","One person may take part in a maximum of three single events and two group events.","Proof of age: all participants must carry an age verification ID (a copy or photo of a passport, birth certificate or similar). It may have to be shown at the chest number desk. Random checks are made. Chest numbers are not given if proof is not shown. The responsibility rests with the participant and the parents or guardians.","The association must certify that the family is a member of the association and lives locally, and that the date of birth was checked against a passport, birth certificate or driving licence."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to register","Items":["Entries for Kalamela 2022 are fully electronic. The participant's association must collect the completed declaration forms and enter the details on the Kalamela web portal ({{EntryPortal}}) for the Regional Kalamela.","Regional winners are registered automatically for the National Kalamela.","Associations get their login details from the regional committee. Regional committees get theirs from the national Kalamela convenor. A user guide ('How to use Kalamela software') is given to authorised users.","Use separate registration forms for single items and group items.","Each form has a declaration by the participant (or parent if under 18, or the team leader for group items) agreeing to the terms and conditions, and giving UUKMA the right to use photographs for general purposes.","Check the spelling of names before submitting, because the full name on the form is printed on certificates.","On request, the participant must show an ID proof of age. Failing to do so may risk participation.","The single form asks for chest number (office use), full name, gender, date of birth, item names (single 1 to 3), category (Kids, Sub-Juniors, Juniors, Seniors), association, region, contact number and email. The group form asks for the item, category, association, region, team manager contact and email, and full name, date of birth and parent's signature (if a minor) for each participant."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Regional and National rounds","Items":["Each association can send three entries for each individual item and each group item to the Regional Kalamela.","Each region can send three entries for each individual item and each group item to the National Kalamela.","If a region has more than three entries (for example two firsts and two seconds), the regional committee sorts this out at regional level. The national committee accepts only three entries.","The Regional Kalamela and the National Kalamela are both run under this manual."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Group sizes","Items":["Group items: at least 3 and at most 8 participants.","Exceptions: Oppana, Thiruvathira and Margamkali allow up to 10 participants. Mime allows 4 to 6 participants.","The item list also prints Group Song and Nadan Pattukal (folk song) as 3 to 10 members."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["The manual prints no entry fee.","Complaint (review) fee: {{ComplaintFee}}."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["The National Kalamela date given in the foreword is {{NationalDate}}."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The National Kalamela venue given in the foreword is {{NationalVenue}}."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"On the day","Items":["A strict time schedule is kept all day.","Chest numbers are given in the morning of the event.","Contestants must report to the stage manager 30 minutes before their stage time. Contestants who fail to do so risk not getting a chance to perform.","The stage arrangement is the participants' own responsibility.","A maximum of 4 minutes in total is allowed to set up and clear the stage. Contact the stage manager early for clarification.","Participants must not use anything that spoils the stage floor, and must clear any spill for the next performer or team.","Background music or track music (where the rules allow it) must be recorded on a memory stick and given to the stage manager at least 30 minutes before the item.","Organisers are not responsible for any fault in the music supplied by contestants. Bring backup music. Playing from mobile phones is not recommended.","Make-up and costumes: classical dance costumes must suit the classical style. For Mime, make-up is for the face only and a white base is preferred."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judgement and results","Items":["Judging follows set criteria for every event. The criteria are given to the jury before the competition starts.","2 points are deducted by each judge if the performance goes over the maximum time for that event.","The judges' decision is final.","If two or more participants tie in an item, all of them are declared winners.","Judges must make fair and impartial judgements.","Any attempt by parents or office bearers to influence a result must be reported to the UUKMA National President or Secretary.","Participants and parents or guardians must not contact the judges about any judgement issue."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and review","Items":["Questions about judgement on the days of the event go to the Review Committee. It re-checks the tabulation of marks, the terms and conditions, and technical matters for that event.","Performing again or video re-judgement is not allowed. The Review Committee's decision is final.","A complaint must be sent through the association and the regional president or secretary within one hour after the result is announced.","The fee to file a complaint is {{ComplaintFee}}, paid in cash with the appeal form. It is refunded if the review succeeds. If not, it is added to the Kalamela organising fund.","The review form needs the contestant's name, item, chest number, association, region, position, reason, and the signatures of the association president or secretary (support) and the region president or secretary (recommendation). Proof of age is shown at the review.","The review committee checks and verifies age and category, checks the score sheet and result sheet for errors, and looks at other factors in the complaint."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points","Items":["Point allocation for Individual Champions and Overall Championship: Single item 1st / 2nd / 3rd = 5 / 3 / 1 for an individual, and 5 / 3 / 1 for the association or region. Group item 1st / 2nd / 3rd = 1 / 1/2 / 1/4 for an individual, and 10 / 7 / 5 for the association or region.","For Kalathilakam and Kalaprathibha, single items give 5 / 3 / 1 points and group items 1 / 1/2 / 1/4 points for 1st / 2nd / 3rd.","Programmes disqualified by the judges are not counted for points."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Winners and awards","Items":["Trophies or medals and certificates are given to each winner of 1st, 2nd and 3rd place in every competing event.","UUKMA Kalathilakam (for the most versatile female performer) and Kalaprathibha (for the most versatile male performer) honour the most multi-talented performer across all categories. To qualify, a contestant must have won 1st prize in a single dance event and 1st prize in a single non-dance event. If no one qualifies, contestants with a first or second place in single dance and non-dance events are considered. If there is still a tie, group item points are used. If a tie remains, the award is shared. If no one meets the criteria, the organising committee may choose a winner from total scores.","UUKMA Natya Mayooram (National Kalamela only): for a dancer who wins three first prizes in single dance competitions across all categories. If more than one dancer qualifies, the award is shared.","UUKMA Malayalam Bhasha Kesari Puraskaram (National Kalamela only): for the person with the most points in Malayalam Elocution, Malayalam Padyam Chollal (poem recitation), Monoact and Malayalam Story Telling across all categories. There are no separate awards for male and female. A tie shares the award.","One Individual Champion award in each age category for the most points from single items (not separate for male and female). A tie is decided by group points, and then shared.","Overall Championship: in the Regional Kalamela, the associations with the most and second most points get the Championship Winner Association and Runners Up Association ever-rolling trophies. In the National Kalamela, the associations and regions with the most and second most points get the Championship Winner and Runners Up ever-rolling trophies."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other items in the manual","Items":["Monoact (Malayalam) is a solo item: one person plays different characters with different tones, styles, dialogue and expressions. No costume per character is needed. Time 5 minutes for Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors. This template does not carry it.","Mime: acting on a theme or story without words. No microphones. Background music with no words is allowed. Face make-up only, white base preferred. No offensive, obscene or disrespectful actions or gestures. 4 to 6 participants, 5 minutes. This template does not carry it.","Nadan Pattukal (folk song), group of 3 to 10 members, 5 minutes in the item list. One thappu may be used. This template does not carry it.","Super Seniors (above 35) have one group item, Group Cinematic Dance. This template does not carry the category.","Katha Prasangam and Fancy Dress are named in the template but are not printed in this manual.","Ages in this manual are as on 1 September 2022. The foreword is signed by the President, General Secretary and Co-ordinator of the UUKMA National Committee."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022","Url":"https://www.uukma.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/UUKMA-Kalamela-Manual-2022-3.pdf"}]}`),t=[],i=[{AgeGroup:"Kids",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories and List of items (Kids)",Sections:{About:["Age 8 years and below, born on or after 1 September 2014."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Kids items: Solo Song (Malayalam or English, 5 minutes), Story Telling (Malayalam or English, 4 minutes), Cinematic Dance Solo (5 minutes) and Group Cinematic Dance (8 members, 7 minutes)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Age 8 years and below, born on or after 1 September 2014.

## Rules
- Kids items: Solo Song (Malayalam or English, 5 minutes), Story Telling (Malayalam or English, 4 minutes), Cinematic Dance Solo (5 minutes) and Group Cinematic Dance (8 members, 7 minutes).`},{AgeGroup:"Sub Juniors",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories",Sections:{About:["Above 8 and up to 12 years, born 1 September 2010 to 31 August 2014 (both dates included)."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Sub-Juniors may enter Malayalam or English Elocution, but not both."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Above 8 and up to 12 years, born 1 September 2010 to 31 August 2014 (both dates included).

## Rules
- Sub-Juniors may enter Malayalam or English Elocution, but not both.`},{AgeGroup:"Juniors",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories",Sections:{About:["Above 12 and up to 17 years, born 1 September 2005 to 31 August 2010 (both dates included)."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Juniors may enter Malayalam or English Elocution, but not both."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Above 12 and up to 17 years, born 1 September 2005 to 31 August 2010 (both dates included).

## Rules
- Juniors may enter Malayalam or English Elocution, but not both.`},{AgeGroup:"Seniors",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories",Sections:{About:["Above 17 years, born on or before 31 August 2005."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["There is no English Elocution for Seniors."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Above 17 years, born on or before 31 August 2005.

## Rules
- There is no English Elocution for Seniors.`},{AgeGroup:"Common",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories and List of items (Common)",Sections:{About:["Any age; no age limit."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Common items: Mime, Group Song, Thiruvathira, Oppana, Margamkali and Nadan Pattukal."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Any age; no age limit.

## Rules
- Common items: Mime, Group Song, Thiruvathira, Oppana, Margamkali and Nadan Pattukal.`}],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Singing","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Kids list and criteria 1","Sections":{"About":["Matched to the manual's Kids Solo Song (Malayalam or English)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Solo song is performed without track or background music.","For Kids, any Malayalam or English song can be chosen."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 25, Flow and expression 25, Stage confidence and presentation 20, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Matched to the manual's Kids Solo Song (Malayalam or English).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Solo song is performed without track or background music.\\n- For Kids, any Malayalam or English song can be chosen.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 25, Flow and expression 25, Stage confidence and presentation 20, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Story Telling","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines, Kids list and criteria 2","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Story Telling is now conducted for Kids only. It can be in English or in Malayalam."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 25, Flow and expression 25, Stage confidence and presentation 20, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Story Telling is now conducted for Kids only. It can be in English or in Malayalam.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 25, Flow and expression 25, Stage confidence and presentation 20, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 3","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Sub-Juniors and Juniors can take part in either the Malayalam or the English elocution competition, but not both.","There is no English elocution for Seniors.","For Sub-Juniors and Juniors, one topic is announced 7 days in advance.","For Seniors, two selected topics are announced on the morning of the competition. One is chosen by toss before the competition. Contestants are told 5 minutes before their slot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Introduction and speech construction 15, Presentation and delivery 15, Content (relevance to the topic) 30, Language and vocal inclination 25, Stage confidence and overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Sub-Juniors and Juniors can take part in either the Malayalam or the English elocution competition, but not both.\\n- There is no English elocution for Seniors.\\n- For Sub-Juniors and Juniors, one topic is announced 7 days in advance.\\n- For Seniors, two selected topics are announced on the morning of the competition. One is chosen by toss before the competition. Contestants are told 5 minutes before their slot.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Introduction and speech construction 15, Presentation and delivery 15, Content (relevance to the topic) 30, Language and vocal inclination 25, Stage confidence and overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Solo Song","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines, item list and criteria 5","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Performed without track or background music.","To promote the Malayalam language and to make judging easier, it is Malayalam light music only (Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors).","Film songs are not allowed in Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Fluency 15, Sruthilayam 25, Rhythm and clarity 25, Bhavam 25, Overall impression 10."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Performed without track or background music.\\n- To promote the Malayalam language and to make judging easier, it is Malayalam light music only (Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors).\\n- Film songs are not allowed in Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Fluency 15, Sruthilayam 25, Rhythm and clarity 25, Bhavam 25, Overall impression 10."},{"Title":"Poem Recitation","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 4","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Poem Recitation (Padyam Chollal) must be in Malayalam.","It is an event for Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 30, Flow and expression 30, Stage confidence and presentation 15, Overall impression 10."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Poem Recitation (Padyam Chollal) must be in Malayalam.\\n- It is an event for Sub-Juniors, Juniors and Seniors.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Memorisation and delivery 15, Literacy clarity 30, Flow and expression 30, Stage confidence and presentation 15, Overall impression 10."},{"Title":"Bharathanatyam","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 7","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Traditional classical songs or music must be used.","The costume must suit the classical dance style.","Songs from films are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm (Nritta, Nritya, Natya) 25, Presentation, postures and perfection of mudras (Adavu, Mudra, Angasudhi) 30, Sense of space and overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Traditional classical songs or music must be used.\\n- The costume must suit the classical dance style.\\n- Songs from films are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm (Nritta, Nritya, Natya) 25, Presentation, postures and perfection of mudras (Adavu, Mudra, Angasudhi) 30, Sense of space and overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Mohiniyattam","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 8","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Traditional classical songs or music must be used.","The costume must suit the classical dance style.","Songs from films are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm (Nritta, Nritya, Natya) 25, Presentation, postures and perfection of mudras (Adavu, Mudra, Angasudhi) 30, Sense of space and overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Traditional classical songs or music must be used.\\n- The costume must suit the classical dance style.\\n- Songs from films are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm (Nritta, Nritya, Natya) 25, Presentation, postures and perfection of mudras (Adavu, Mudra, Angasudhi) 30, Sense of space and overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Folk Dance","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 9","Sections":{"About":["Folk dance is performed for every possible occasion: the arrival of seasons, the birth of a child, a wedding and festivals. It is very simple, with few steps or movements, and should suit the child's age. The skill and imagination of the dancer shape the performance."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 7 minutes."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Expression, power and use of stage 25, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Folk dance is performed for every possible occasion: the arrival of seasons, the birth of a child, a wedding and festivals. It is very simple, with few steps or movements, and should suit the child's age. The skill and imagination of the dancer shape the performance.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 7 minutes.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Expression, power and use of stage 25, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Cinematic Dance","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 10","Sections":{"About":["Cinematic or free style dance (single and group)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Solo: maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Pure classical or semi-classical dances are not allowed. Semi-classical dance styles may form a part of the dance.","Apart from this, there are no rules. Vocal or instrumental music may be used and need not be from films."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm 25, Use of stage, power and dynamics 25, Overall impression 15, Use of properties 5."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Cinematic or free style dance (single and group).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Solo: maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Pure classical or semi-classical dances are not allowed. Semi-classical dance styles may form a part of the dance.\\n- Apart from this, there are no rules. Vocal or instrumental music may be used and need not be from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Movement and rhythm 25, Use of stage, power and dynamics 25, Overall impression 15, Use of properties 5."},{"Title":"Group Dance (Cinematic or Non-Classical)","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines, item list and criteria 12","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The guidelines and item list give 7 minutes. The criteria table gives a maximum of 10 minutes."],"Rules":["3 to 8 participants (Kids group: 8 members).","Pure classical or semi-classical dances are not allowed. Semi-classical dance styles may form a part of the dance.","Vocal or instrumental music may be used and need not be from films."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Synchronisation and group formation 25, Power and dynamics 25, Overall impression 15, Use of properties 5."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The guidelines and item list give 7 minutes. The criteria table gives a maximum of 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- 3 to 8 participants (Kids group: 8 members).\\n- Pure classical or semi-classical dances are not allowed. Semi-classical dance styles may form a part of the dance.\\n- Vocal or instrumental music may be used and need not be from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 20, Synchronisation and group formation 25, Power and dynamics 25, Overall impression 15, Use of properties 5."},{"Title":"Classical Dance (Group)","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 13","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Any known form of Indian classical dance may be performed purely or in fusion form.","3 to 8 participants."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Any known form of Indian classical dance may be performed purely or in fusion form.\\n- 3 to 8 participants.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Group Song","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines, item list and criteria 11","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The guidelines and item list give 5 minutes. The criteria table gives 7 minutes."],"Rules":["Must be in Malayalam.","Performed without track or background music.","Film songs and devotional songs are not allowed.","At least 3 members. The guidelines say at most 8 members; the item list and criteria say at most 10."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Pitch and modulation 15, Sruthilayam 25, Rhythm 25, Bhavam and literacy clarity 25, Overall impression 10."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The guidelines and item list give 5 minutes. The criteria table gives 7 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Must be in Malayalam.\\n- Performed without track or background music.\\n- Film songs and devotional songs are not allowed.\\n- At least 3 members. The guidelines say at most 8 members; the item list and criteria say at most 10.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Pitch and modulation 15, Sruthilayam 25, Rhythm 25, Bhavam and literacy clarity 25, Overall impression 10."},{"Title":"Thiruvathira","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 14","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Females only. At most 10 members.","Songs can be traditional or from films."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Females only. At most 10 members.\\n- Songs can be traditional or from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Oppana","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 16","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Females only. At most 10 members.","Songs can be traditional or from films."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Females only. At most 10 members.\\n- Songs can be traditional or from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."},{"Title":"Margam Kali","Source":"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, General guidelines and criteria 15","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Females only. At most 10 members.","Songs can be traditional or from films."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Females only. At most 10 members.\\n- Songs can be traditional or from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgement criteria (manual pages 13-16), maximum marks: Costume and visual appeal 10, Music and choreography 25, Movement and rhythm 25, Stage use, presentation and synchronisation 25, Overall impression 15."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"AgeAsOn",Kind:"date",Label:"Age is taken as on",Value:"2022-09-01",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Age categories"},{Key:"NationalDate",Kind:"date",Label:"National Kalamela date",Value:"2022-11-05",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, foreword (translated from Malayalam)"},{Key:"NationalVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"National Kalamela venue",Value:{Name:"To be announced (the foreword says Cheltenham)",Address:"",City:"Cheltenham",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, foreword"},{Key:"EntryPortal",Kind:"link",Label:"Kalamela web portal for entries",Value:"www.uukmakalamela.co.uk",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Main changes"},{Key:"ComplaintFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Complaint / review fee",Value:"GBP 25, paid in cash with the appeal form; refunded if the review succeeds",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, Complaints and review form"},{Key:"NationalCommittee",Kind:"contact",Label:"UUKMA National Committee officers named in the foreword",Value:{Name:"Dr Biju Peringathara (President), Kuryan George (General Secretary), Jayakumar Nair (Co-ordinator)",Role:"UUKMA National Committee",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022, foreword"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, categories, items, criteria, awards and points as printed in the 2022 Kalamela Manual",SourceType:"Primary - UUKMA's own Kalamela Manual",Source:"UUKMA Kalamela Manual 2022",Url:"https://www.uukma.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/UUKMA-Kalamela-Manual-2022-3.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2022,Note:a,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,a as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,m as Year,u as default};
